WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.434
-Welcome to the show.
They love you.

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:03.601
-Hi, guys!
-Yeah!

00:00:03.601 --> 00:00:06.000
We love you. It is great
to see you in the flesh.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.567
We've only Zoomed.
-I know.

00:00:07.567 --> 00:00:10.067
-Yeah, you're just as gorgeous
and stunning

00:00:10.067 --> 00:00:12.501
as you were on Zoom.
-We're not catfishes.

00:00:12.501 --> 00:00:13.634
-No, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:13.634 --> 00:00:14.834
No, we're not.
We're real people.

00:00:14.834 --> 00:00:17.033
-Yeah.
-Thanksgiving is tomorrow.

00:00:17.033 --> 00:00:19.133
Happy Thanksgiving early.
-Happy Thanksgiving.

00:00:19.133 --> 00:00:20.834
-Jacques Pépin
and I are cooking later.

00:00:20.834 --> 00:00:23.801
Do you have a specialty
Thanksgiving dish?

00:00:23.801 --> 00:00:25.434
-No. No.
-Oh, okay.

00:00:25.434 --> 00:00:27.267
-I don't cook.
-At all?

00:00:27.267 --> 00:00:29.934
-No, it's within everybody's
best interest if I don't.

00:00:29.934 --> 00:00:31.400
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, I don't think so.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:35.100
Have you ever tried?
-I mean, of course I've tried.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:38.467
But I -- from an early age,
I realized I probably shouldn't.

00:00:38.467 --> 00:00:42.601
I nearly burnt down
my mom's oven.

00:00:42.601 --> 00:00:45.400
Uh, I tried to make cupcakes.

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:46.834
[ Laughter ]
Some chocolate cupcakes.

00:00:46.834 --> 00:00:48.701
But I didn't realize that you
needed, like, I don't know,

00:00:48.701 --> 00:00:52.434
baking soda or baking flour.
So, I like -- it just blew up.

00:00:52.434 --> 00:00:53.868
[ Laughter ]
And from then on,

00:00:53.868 --> 00:00:54.968
she didn't let me --
-You just thought you would

00:00:54.968 --> 00:00:56.634
invent a recipe
and see if it worked?

00:00:56.634 --> 00:00:57.834
-Correct.
-Wow.

00:00:57.834 --> 00:00:59.634
-I know. It's kind of --
it's like this game...

00:00:59.634 --> 00:01:01.167
-What did you put in there?
Do you remember?

00:01:01.167 --> 00:01:02.734
-Oh, yes.
Um cocoa...

00:01:02.734 --> 00:01:04.267
-Uh-huh.
Write this down, everybody.

00:01:04.267 --> 00:01:05.834
[ Laughter ]
-Swiss Miss.

00:01:05.834 --> 00:01:07.834
-Swiss Miss cocoa?
-Yeah, Swiss Miss.

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:08.868
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:10.434
-You are awesome.
That's so funny.

00:01:10.434 --> 00:01:12.100
And it didn't work?
-Delicious.

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:13.868
-No, it's great.
Hot cocoa, yeah.

00:01:13.868 --> 00:01:16.400
-Marshmallows, for texture.
-Yeah.

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:18.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.033 --> 00:01:20.534
Oh, my God.
This is a fire hazard.

00:01:20.534 --> 00:01:22.167
It really is.
-Some flour...

00:01:22.167 --> 00:01:23.934
-Oh, my gosh.
-...and a little bit

00:01:23.934 --> 00:01:26.467
of, um, vegetable oil.

00:01:26.467 --> 00:01:29.167
-Oh, man, it sounds delicious.
Oh, my gosh.

00:01:29.167 --> 00:01:31.167
Next Thanksgiving,
I'm inviting you over.

00:01:31.167 --> 00:01:33.968
-You should, you should.
I can make ramen now.

00:01:33.968 --> 00:01:35.167
-Oh!
-I will make --

00:01:35.167 --> 00:01:37.634
-That's how
we're buddies for life, yeah.

00:01:37.634 --> 00:01:39.567
If you can make ramen,
we're buddies for life.

00:01:39.567 --> 00:01:44.100
-I can do some late-night ramen.
That's my [bleep] -- sorry.

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:45.133
That's my --
That's my...

00:01:45.133 --> 00:01:47.501
[ Laughter ]
...signature dish. Sorry.

00:01:47.501 --> 00:01:49.334
-No problem, no problem.
-I told my dad beforehand --

00:01:49.334 --> 00:01:50.734
-Maybe we should be back
on Zoom.

00:01:50.734 --> 00:01:52.067
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.067 --> 00:01:53.400
We can edit.
-Yeah.

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:55.567
I called my dad beforehand
to tell him it was coming,

00:01:55.567 --> 00:01:57.601
and he said,
"Watch your four-letter words."

00:01:57.601 --> 00:01:58.767
-[ Gasps ]
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.767 --> 00:01:59.934
And you were thinking
of the other one.

00:01:59.934 --> 00:02:02.901
-Sorry, Dad.
-So you slipped with that one.

00:02:02.901 --> 00:02:04.868
'Cause it's the worse one.
-It's the worst one.

00:02:04.868 --> 00:02:06.567
-
-Yeah, but you started
with the kind of best --

00:02:06.567 --> 00:02:09.000
kind of bad one, yeah.
-It's like the PG-13 one.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:10.367
-Yeah.
And then, yeah.

00:02:10.367 --> 00:02:11.467
All right.
So no more of that.

00:02:11.467 --> 00:02:13.934
-No, none of that.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:13.934 --> 00:02:15.767
-But I want
to know more about you.

00:02:15.767 --> 00:02:17.067
You're from South Carolina,
right?

00:02:17.067 --> 00:02:19.501
-I am. I'm from a little town
called Goose Creek.

00:02:19.501 --> 00:02:21.067
-Goose Creek?
-Goose Creek.

00:02:21.067 --> 00:02:22.667
-What a cute name.
-I know.

00:02:22.667 --> 00:02:24.534
-I never heard of Goose Creek.
-But there's -- I mean --

00:02:24.534 --> 00:02:27.634
I don't know if -- I don't think
there's a lot of geese there.

00:02:27.634 --> 00:02:29.801
[ Laughter ]
-Are there creeks there?

00:02:29.801 --> 00:02:31.534
-There's a creek, but I've never
seen any geese in it.

00:02:31.534 --> 00:02:33.234
-No.
-No.

00:02:33.234 --> 00:02:35.033
So, whatever.
You know?

00:02:35.033 --> 00:02:36.167
Hey.
-Either way, cute name.

00:02:36.167 --> 00:02:37.167
I love it.
I'll take it.

00:02:37.167 --> 00:02:39.767
It's like a CW town.
-Yeah.

00:02:39.767 --> 00:02:40.968
No way.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.968 --> 00:02:44.767
Did you have that type
of childhood, upbringing?

00:02:44.767 --> 00:02:46.834
-Very, very suburbia.

00:02:46.834 --> 00:02:48.667
Grew up across the street
from a church.

00:02:48.667 --> 00:02:51.467
-Oh, yeah.
-Mom's a real-estate agent.

00:02:51.467 --> 00:02:53.968
Dad is a civil engineer.
-Wow.

00:02:53.968 --> 00:02:57.400
-And I chose to do everything
they told me not to.

00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:59.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:01.601
-As a child does.
-As one does.

00:03:01.601 --> 00:03:05.667
-But you started acting and you
landed working commercials,

00:03:05.667 --> 00:03:08.634
which a lot of child actors
get their start.

00:03:08.634 --> 00:03:11.067
In fact, we found one of them.

00:03:11.067 --> 00:03:12.968
[ Laughter ]

00:03:12.968 --> 00:03:14.968
I don't know if you know
that we have this.

00:03:14.968 --> 00:03:16.567
Dad, I hope you're watching.

00:03:16.567 --> 00:03:18.133
-Which one?
-I want to show --

00:03:18.133 --> 00:03:21.634
Here's Madelyn Cline
in a commercial...

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:23.901
for a Chuck E. Cheese
Pizza Maker.

00:03:23.901 --> 00:03:25.834
Take a look at this.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:25.834 --> 00:03:28.000
-Today, we're making
Chuck E. Cheese pizza!

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:29.767
-Microwave for just a minute.

00:03:29.767 --> 00:03:31.334
Blend the sauce and cheese.

00:03:31.334 --> 00:03:32.467
Microwave again.

00:03:32.467 --> 00:03:34.767
-Fun food in minutes!

00:03:34.767 --> 00:03:36.734
-And you made real
Chuck E. Cheese pizza

00:03:36.734 --> 00:03:38.367
with EZ-2 Make!

00:03:38.367 --> 00:03:40.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:41.234
-It looks delicious.

00:03:41.234 --> 00:03:43.367
-You know, um...

00:03:43.367 --> 00:03:45.501
-It looks really delicious.

00:03:45.501 --> 00:03:46.834
-You know, uh...

00:03:46.834 --> 00:03:48.434
Have you ever -- you've had
a Lunchable, I'm sure.

00:03:48.434 --> 00:03:50.801
-Yes.
-It's like that, the same thing.

00:03:50.801 --> 00:03:53.601
-You were ahead of your time.
-There's no baking involved.

00:03:53.601 --> 00:03:54.868
-No.
-It's just a turntable.

00:03:54.868 --> 00:03:56.801
-The Chuck E. Cheese pizza maker
is a Lunchable.

00:03:56.801 --> 00:03:57.968
-It is a Lunchable.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.968 --> 00:03:59.467
-There's a lawsuit
happening right now.

00:03:59.467 --> 00:04:01.067
[ Laughter ]

00:04:01.067 --> 00:04:02.634
That's kind of a big deal.
That's great.

00:04:02.634 --> 00:04:04.667
Now look at you.
You're in "Glass Onion."

00:04:04.667 --> 00:04:06.300
-I know.
-You're in a giant movie.

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:08.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:08.601 --> 00:04:11.667
The second installment
of the "Knives Out" franchise.

00:04:11.667 --> 00:04:13.501
Great cast, by the way.

00:04:13.501 --> 00:04:16.934
-Stacked, packed.
-Stacked and packed,

00:04:16.934 --> 00:04:18.567
smothered, covered --
and, yeah.

00:04:18.567 --> 00:04:20.467
-And smashed.
-And smashed.

00:04:20.467 --> 00:04:22.968
You got Daniel Craig.
-I know.

00:04:22.968 --> 00:04:25.000
-Who I love.
-You have Kate Hudson.

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:26.234
Who I also love.
-The best.

00:04:26.234 --> 00:04:28.033
-Yeah. Who did you have
the most scenes with?

00:04:28.033 --> 00:04:29.868
Well, I guess all of them.
-Oh, God.

00:04:29.868 --> 00:04:32.701
You know, obviously,
I'm on the no-spoiler train.

00:04:32.701 --> 00:04:34.868
-So never mind.
-You know, it's an ensemble.

00:04:34.868 --> 00:04:36.667
It's very --
It's a heavy ensemble.

00:04:36.667 --> 00:04:38.601
-You never need to work
with anyone.

00:04:38.601 --> 00:04:39.868
[ Laughter ]
-I don't work with anyone.

00:04:39.868 --> 00:04:41.267
-You didn't talk to anyone
on the set.

00:04:41.267 --> 00:04:42.934
-I just Zoomed in.
-You didn't see a thing.

00:04:42.934 --> 00:04:44.067
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.067 --> 00:04:46.033
"I didn't see anyone at all."

00:04:46.033 --> 00:04:48.400
No, that's a great way
to set up the movie.

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:50.167
"I never met anyone
in the cast."

00:04:50.167 --> 00:04:51.434
Good.
It keeps everyone guess--

00:04:51.434 --> 00:04:53.100
It is a mystery,
so I don't want to ruin it

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:54.133
for anyone else, either, though.

00:04:54.133 --> 00:04:56.234
-It is so much fun.

00:04:56.234 --> 00:04:58.467
We really leaned into --
I would say we leaned into

00:04:58.467 --> 00:05:03.567
the comedy of it all even more
so this time, which was so fun.

00:05:03.567 --> 00:05:06.734
It's just -- I mean --
And when you have Kathryn Hahn

00:05:06.734 --> 00:05:08.133
on a cast --
-Oh, my gosh

00:05:08.133 --> 00:05:10.467
She is funny --
funny and awesome.

00:05:10.467 --> 00:05:11.901
She's one of my favorite guests.
I love her.

00:05:11.901 --> 00:05:14.501
-Oh, she's the best.
-Also, where did you film this?

00:05:14.501 --> 00:05:16.167
It's gorgeous.
-Greece and Serbia.

00:05:16.167 --> 00:05:18.567
-Come on.
-Greece and Serbia, yeah.

00:05:18.567 --> 00:05:19.968
Can we do "The Tonight Show"
from Greece?

00:05:19.968 --> 00:05:21.868
-Can we go?
Can we do it?

00:05:21.868 --> 00:05:23.167
-Let's do "The Tonight Show"
from Greece.

00:05:23.167 --> 00:05:25.000
If we do it, will you come on?
-Of course I will.

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:26.767
-And we'll just do
a whole "Mamma Mia 3" thing.

00:05:26.767 --> 00:05:28.734
-Oh, my --
Are you kidding me?

00:05:28.734 --> 00:05:30.267
-Right?
-That's my bread and butter.

00:05:30.267 --> 00:05:32.067
-That's my ramen.
Let's do it. Come on!

00:05:32.067 --> 00:05:37.534
-Every single weekend
it was "Mamma Mia," orange pie,

00:05:37.534 --> 00:05:39.934
gin and tonics, and pools.
-Yeah.

00:05:39.934 --> 00:05:41.901
-Oh, I love that.
What is orange pie?

00:05:41.901 --> 00:05:44.601
-Oh, it's a Greek thing.
I sound like a foreign --

00:05:44.601 --> 00:05:46.767
Not a foreign --a student
who studied abroad.

00:05:46.767 --> 00:05:47.968
-Yeah.
-Because I'm like,

00:05:47.968 --> 00:05:49.267
"You wouldn't know.
You wouldn't understand.

00:05:49.267 --> 00:05:51.334
You had to be there."
-Yeah, exactly, yeah.

00:05:51.334 --> 00:05:53.901
Exactly, you're just reading
stuff out of a photo or...

00:05:53.901 --> 00:05:56.100
"Oh, you haven't tried...
orange pie?"

00:05:56.100 --> 00:05:57.901
[ Laughter ]

00:05:57.901 --> 00:05:59.000
-"Judging you."

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:00.167
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:00.167 --> 00:06:02.434
Here's Madelyn Cline
and Janelle Monae

00:06:02.434 --> 00:06:04.901
in "Glass Onion."
Take a look at this.

00:06:04.901 --> 00:06:06.434
-This is my second one
of these things.

00:06:06.434 --> 00:06:09.934
We did a yacht thing last year.
-Well, that sounds fun.

00:06:09.934 --> 00:06:12.167
-[ Chuckles ]
No.

00:06:12.167 --> 00:06:13.734
I mean,
when they're all together,

00:06:13.734 --> 00:06:15.767
it's kind of the worst.

00:06:15.767 --> 00:06:17.200
Duke just treats me
like arm candy,

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:18.601
and they just ignore me.

00:06:18.601 --> 00:06:22.267
-Why do you put up with it?
-With Duke?

00:06:22.267 --> 00:06:24.200
I'm building my brand.

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:27.667
And he's putting me
on his channel more often.

00:06:27.667 --> 00:06:31.133
So he's leaning harder right
into this Mandom stuff.

00:06:31.133 --> 00:06:34.200
Like, if I'm going to go
into politics eventually,

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:35.801
I don't think that's a road
I want to go down.

00:06:35.801 --> 00:06:39.901
Like, it's expeditious,
but it's kind of a [bleep] show.

00:06:39.901 --> 00:06:41.734
Oh.
Here's the pool.

00:06:41.734 --> 00:06:43.334
-I'm gonna walk around
a little longer.

00:06:43.334 --> 00:06:44.968
I'll catch you over there.
-Okay.

00:06:44.968 --> 00:06:47.400
-Hey, it's really great
talking to you, Whiskey.

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:49.634
-You too.

00:06:49.634 --> 00:06:52.133
-Mm!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:52.133 --> 00:06:54.033
Are you?

00:06:54.033 --> 00:06:56.367
Are you, or are you not?

00:06:56.367 --> 00:06:58.133
-Who is she?
-Who is she?

00:06:58.133 --> 00:06:59.267
What is she all about?

00:06:59.267 --> 00:07:01.033
Does she know too much?

00:07:01.033 --> 00:07:02.834
-Or too little?
-Or too little?

00:07:02.834 --> 00:07:04.868
Or is she working on her brand?

00:07:04.868 --> 00:07:06.234
Whoo!
I love it.

00:07:06.234 --> 00:07:07.501
Madelyn Cline, everybody.

00:07:07.501 --> 00:07:09.767
"Glass Onion:
A Knives Out Mystery"

00:07:09.767 --> 00:07:11.133
is in theaters now.

00:07:11.133 --> 00:07:14.133
You can catch it on Netflix
beginning December 23rd.

